      "message": "fix(multiaxis): prove every swarf exit rise with an exact sweep\n\nThe full-band swarf tests failed the release gate with nine RapidInPart\nwarnings. The nine moves were the plan's own retract rapids off each\nside-pass level. The stamp gave each of them the held lying pose with no\nproof, and the flank (or, under the tube's equator, the ball) rose\nthrough the blade.\n\n- stamp_sweep.rs: the exact distance from a tool axis swept along a\n  straight move (a parallelogram) to each facet, by the\n  triangle-triangle distance law.\n- stamp_rise.rs: the rise proof uses that sweep instead of r/2 samples,\n  against the start pose's own gap. A plan rapid rise answers to the\n  same proof. If it is not proved, it leaves along the contact normal\n  under the same pose, then rises, each leg proved. If no exit is\n  proved, it stays the plan's own and the verifier judges it.\n\nFixes #4315\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
